---
import '../styles/prose.css';

import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-10-20T04:22:31Z');
const lastUpdatedDisplay = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  hour: '2-digit',
  minute: '2-digit',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
  timeZoneName: 'short',
}).format(lastUpdated);
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Clear terms for thebytearray.org and our apps: what you get, pay-once price, requirements, updates, support and refunds. Fair deals only. No hidden charges."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Terms', path: '/terms/' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-4 sm:pt-10" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,7.5vw,3.75rem)] leading-[1.04] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance"
      >
        Terms
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-label-lg text-on-surface-variant">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString()}>{lastUpdatedDisplay}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Our promise</h2>
        <p>
          A deal should leave neither side wronged. What is listed on an app page is what you get,
          the price shown at purchase is the full price for that scope, and remedies follow our{' '}
          <a href="/refund-policy/" class="text-link">refund policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <p>
          Each app page lists its features under What it does, its requirements (for example Android
          7.0+), and whether it is free, pay-once or discontinued. Convertit Pro unlocks only the
          tools listed as of 20 October 2026. Future new tools will be listed before any charge.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Price and payment</h2>
        <p>
          Free apps cost nothing. Paid apps are one purchase through Google Play, which handles
          payment and VAT. We never see your payment details. No subscriptions, no ads to remove,
          no in-app charges beyond the listed purchase.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Updates and support</h2>
        <p>
          We fix what we advertise. Contact us with your order number (GPA…), purchase date and
          steps to reproduce. We aim to reply within 5 business days and fix or work around within
          14 business days. Refund timing is in our{' '}
          <a href="/refund-policy/" class="text-link">refund policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Open and closed source</h2>
        <p>
          OpenLoader and this website are {site.license.name}. Convertit, Convertit Pro and Hy2NG
          are closed. See{' '}
          <a href="/blog/why-convertit-is-not-open-source/" class="text-link">why Convertit is not open source</a>.
          Discontinued apps are marked and keep working for existing installs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Site content</h2>
        <p>
          This website is open source under{' '}
          <a href={site.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link">{site.license.name}</a>.
          Downloads list version, size and SHA-256 so you can verify what you install.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms use our{' '}
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or email us at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
